{"actions":[{"actionCode":null,"actionDate":"2026-07-15","source":"Senate","text":"Received in the Senate and Read twice and referred to the Committee on Banking, Housing, and Urban Affairs.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"actionCode":"H38310","actionDate":"2026-07-14","source":"House floor actions","text":"Motion to reconsider laid on the table Agreed to without objection.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H37100","actionDate":"2026-07-14","source":"House floor actions","text":"On passage Passed by the Yeas and Nays: 221 - 201 (Roll no. 240). (text: CR H4441-4442)","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"8000","actionDate":"2026-07-14","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Passed/agreed to in House: On passage Passed by the Yeas and Nays: 221 - 201 (Roll no. 240).","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H36210","actionDate":"2026-07-14","source":"House floor actions","text":"On motion to recommit Failed by the Yeas and Nays: 208 - 217 (Roll no. 239).","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H30000","actionDate":"2026-07-14","source":"House floor actions","text":"Considered as unfinished business. (consideration: CR H4451-4452)","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H8D000","actionDate":"2026-07-14","source":"House floor actions","text":"POSTPONED PROCEEDINGS - At the conclusion of debate on H.R. 1181 the Chair put the question on the motion to recommit and by voice vote, announced the noes had prevailed. Mr. Frost demanded the yeas and nays and the Chair postponed further proceedings until a time to be announced.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H8A000","actionDate":"2026-07-14","source":"House floor actions","text":"The previous question on the motion to recommit was ordered pursuant to clause 2(b) of rule XIX.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H36200","actionDate":"2026-07-14","source":"House floor actions","text":"Mr. Frost moved to recommit to the Committee on Financial Services. (CR H4445)","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H35000","actionDate":"2026-07-14","source":"House floor actions","text":"The previous question was ordered pursuant to the rule.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H8D000","actionDate":"2026-07-14","source":"House floor actions","text":"DEBATE - The House proceeded with one hour of debate on H.R. 1181.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H8D000","actionDate":"2026-07-14","source":"House floor actions","text":"Rule provides for consideration of H.R. 139, H.R. 8595, H.R. 9237 and H.R. 1181. The resolution provides for consideration of H.R. 139, H.R. 9237, and H.R. 1181 under a closed rule, and H.R. 8595 under a structured rule with one hour of debate and one motion to reconsider on each bill.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H30000","actionDate":"2026-07-14","source":"House floor actions","text":"Considered under the provisions of rule H. Res. 1423. (consideration: CR H4441-4445)","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H1L220","actionDate":"2026-07-14","source":"House floor actions","text":"Rule H. Res. 1423 passed House.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H1L210","actionDate":"2026-07-13","source":"House floor actions","text":"Rules Committee Resolution H. Res. 1423 Reported to House. Rule provides for consideration of H.R. 139, H.R. 8595, H.R. 9237 and H.R. 1181. The resolution provides for consideration of H.R. 139, H.R. 9237, and H.R. 1181 under a closed rule, and H.R. 8595 under a structured rule with one hour of debate and one motion to reconsider on each bill.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H1L210","actionDate":"2026-06-23","source":"House floor actions","text":"Rules Committee Resolution H. Res. 1377 Reported to House. Rule provides for consideration of H.R. 1181, H.R. 9022, H.R. 8595 and H.R. 9237. The resolution provides for consideration of H.R. 1181 and H.R. 9237 under a closed rule and H.R. 9022 and H.R. 8595 under a structured rule. The resolution provides for one hour of general debate and one motion to recommit on each bill.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H12410","actionDate":"2026-02-25","source":"House floor actions","text":"Placed on the Union C